message: >-
  If you refer to this study, its code or its artefacts, please cite the
  repository using the metadata below. No DOI has been minted; cite the release
  tag, or the commit hash if you are referring to a specific state of the tree.
title: "Council: a placebo-controlled study of whether language models hold their ground"
abstract: >-
  Four open-weight models judge the same market question independently, then
  again in committee. A placebo arm feeds each reader a real peer argument about
  an unrelated day, and a coherent-contradictor arm feeds it three peers arguing
  against its own view on its own data, so that reacting to an argument can be
  separated from reacting to being contradicted. The finding is that opposition
  dose, not argument content, predicts whether an agent abandons its position --
  reproduced independently inside the genuine debate arm's own dose-response --
  and that the same models almost never capitulate on questions with verifiable
  answers. The repository carries the pre-registration, every decision artefact,
  a register of 31 numbered claims and 17 defects including the ones that
  falsified its own headlines, and tests that recompute each published figure
  from the artefacts.
